{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J2 62d9 PLAN REVIEW #2 -> PASS (0 blocking, 1 advisory: generic P6 impact 0.4, skipped). CLAIMED 62d9 (assignee RebarBotNava), phase now execution.\n\nJ2 ORACLE AUTHORED AND CONFIRMED RED (Phase 4b). Three new files, 3 test tiers:\n (HAPPY PATH — the ONLY file the implementer will see) tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_family_seam.py, 16 tests pinning the new jira_family PUBLIC surface: both value maps (incl. unified deleted->Done), RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK incl. the three deliberately-ABSENT relations, label sanitizer at inclusive 255 + all four rejection reasons, summary sanitizer at inclusive 254 vs 255-truncates (the deliberate off-by-one), the two contract-parameterized sanitizers proving the vendor dep is INJECTED not imported, the identity convention incl. the legacy hyphen read-form, and the probe classifier with the resolved-status set injected.\n (HELD OUT) test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py, 17 tests: AST import-graph contract over every engine module (shared layer <- concrete backends, one direction); jira_family imports NO Cloud vendor module; no re-export shim at any pre-move path; exactly ONE dict literal per value map within adapters/ AND both Cloud callers resolving to it by IDENTITY (not equality — identity is what actually proves de-duplication); the three location-pinned paths unmoved; and by-path spec_from_file_location loads proving the new imports are ABSOLUTE.\n (HELD OUT) test_acli_status_resolution_heldout.py, 8 tests driving the REAL production entry point acli.transition_issue with a fake transport, asserting both the contractual return value and the name actually sent.\n\nRED EVIDENCE:\n - seam.py: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira_family' (genuine absence — the package is this story's deliverable).\n - boundary_heldout: 9 failed / 8 passed. Failures all for the right reason: package absent; jira_fields.py still binds _LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA/_LOCAL_PRIORITY_TO_JIRA/_RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK; identity.py still present; TWO status-map literals and TWO priority-map literals found under adapters/ (the exact pre-existing duplication the story deletes).\n - acli_status_heldout: 1 failed / 7 passed, and the failure is the money shot — 'assert Deleted == Done'. That empirically CONFIRMS the latent bug the plan reasoned about: the ACLI path really does resolve deleted -> the invalid 'Deleted' today. The 7 passing are the contrast cases (every other status resolves unchanged + the .title() fallback), which must KEEP passing.\n\nTEST DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED DURING RED (my own, not the implementer's): test_checker_flags_a_synthetic_violation initially FAILED. Cause was in the TEST, not the checker — I passed package strings one level too deep (_FAMILY.fields instead of _FAMILY), which broke the relative-import arithmetic for 'from ..jira import adf'. Fixed the synthetic inputs to what _package_of actually yields and added an 'import X' spelling plus two more negative controls. It now passes, which is correct: it exercises the checker, not production code, so it is teeth rather than an oracle.\nNOTE ON NON-RED TESTS: 8 boundary tests pass pre-implementation by construction — the 3 pinned-path collateral invariants and the by-path outbound_fields load (things that must NOT change), the checker-teeth test, and 2 graph assertions that are vacuous while jira_family is absent (deliberately guarded by test_jira_family_package_exists, which is RED). Recorded rather than 'fixed': a collateral invariant that passes before and after is doing its job."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785342009496491001,"uuid":"e33132a1-6a2e-447b-8f51-e2f7ec53fcb9"}